From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:38:31 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/30] SWGL samples video frames on the GPU where they were
 decoded

With frames staying on the GPU, the Lumia 650 decoded 30 frames a second
but showed about 10: the frames were not promoted to compositor surfaces
(RGB images only ever try an overlay), so SWGL drew them from
RenderDXGITextureHost::MapPlane, which made a staging texture, copied the
frame into it and waited on the GPU for every frame, and then uploaded the
pixels again. SwglGpuSetTextureSource now makes a SWGL texture a BGRA
Direct3D texture on its own device, which GPU draws sample in place (CPU
draws read it back if they must); RenderTextureHostSWGL uses it for DXGI
frames on the compositor's device before falling back to mapping. The log
says once which way video frames are drawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
